      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-321774",
      ":question/problem": "In triangles $GHI$ and $JKL$, angles $H$ and $K$ each have measure $35^{\u2218}$ and angles $I$ and $L$ each have measure $48^{\u2218}$. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that triangle $GHI$ is congruent to triangle $JKL$?\n\n1. The length of side $GH^(\u2015)$.\n2. The measure of angle $G$.\n3. The lengths of sides $HI^(\u2015)$ and $KL^(\u2015)$.\n4. No additional information is needed."
