      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-321792",
      ":question/problem": "In triangles $CDM$ and $ABF$, angles $C$ and $A$ each have measure $58^{\u2218}$, and angles $D$ and $B$ each have measure $58^{\u2218}$. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that triangle $CDM$ is congruent to triangle $ABF$?\n\n1. The measures of $\u2220M$ and $\u2220F$ are equal.\n2. The lengths of $DM^(\u2015)$ and $BF^(\u2015)$ are equal.\n3. The lengths of $CM^(\u2015)$ and $AF^(\u2015)$ are equal.\n4. No additional information is needed."
